I went through one of those

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:28.860
really tough seasons that's
kind of waiting for everybody,

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.620
you know, if you haven't
been through it yet,

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.086
just wait is coming, you know?

00:08:33.086 --> 00:08:33.919
- Yeah.
- But, you know,

00:08:33.919 --> 00:08:35.790
one of those seasons and I
journaled through the whole thing

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:38.220
and I really was just
honestly trying to make it

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:39.870
to the other side of that.
- Yeah.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.970
- And I never was thinking

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.850
that I would use it creatively in any way,

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.040
but yeah, there, it dawned on me

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.830
this one day as I was listening to music

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:51.540
and, you know music was such a balm

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.277
and such a guiding light.

00:08:54.277 --> 00:08:55.395
- Oh yeah.
- [Leslie] Through that time

00:08:55.395 --> 00:08:56.460
it was like always...
- Healing.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.260
- I'm supposed to use this,

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.300
I'm supposed to write about this,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.160
you know, I'm supposed to make the record

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.740
that I needed to listen to, you know,

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:06.035
about going through this.

00:09:06.035 --> 00:09:08.927
- Oh yeah that's like the goal, right?

00:09:08.927 --> 00:09:11.250
That's something you would
want to get through as well.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.700
Like, well, when Leslie actually
was making his album, "Mr"

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:15.967
he wrote in his journal,

00:09:15.967 --> 00:09:17.340
"Finish the Task...

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.080
God needs some folks who are willing

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.690
and courageous enough to
finish what they started,

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.220
especially after he starts them."

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.420
- [Leslie] Right.
- I love that.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:25.957
- Yeah.
- It's so beautiful.

00:09:25.957 --> 00:09:26.985
(audience clapping and cheering loudly)

00:09:26.985 --> 00:09:29.717
Do you feel like that still resonates?

00:09:29.717 --> 00:09:31.950
- Yeah, I mean, every now and again that,

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:35.400
because the journey's long,
you know, it's a long journey

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.670
and you can lose your way
sometimes in the middle.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.500
So I wrote that, that down

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.500
because I needed to remember
it, you know, I needed to...

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.789
- Almost remind yourself, yeah.

00:09:44.789 --> 00:09:45.622
- That's right.

00:09:45.622 --> 00:09:50.520
That it's like, it's not
always about judging yourself

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.220
and what you think is good
and what you think is worthy.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.260
Finish it, finish the task.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.660
You know, the inspiration is holy,

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.280
the inspiration to
start something I think,

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.360
you know, those things are like,

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.100
they come from somewhere and to

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.260
honor that original inspiration,

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.790
and the least you can do is
finish the task as best you can.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.386
- Yeah, thank you, (audience
clapping and cheering loudly)

00:10:11.386 --> 00:10:14.634
I agree with that, so tell
me about your new album.

00:10:14.634 --> 00:10:15.467
This is...

00:10:15.467 --> 00:10:16.830
I was listening to it all last night

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:19.680
it's different like, than
what I'm used to like hearing,

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.120
but it's so cool, it's different.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.040
It's got, and especially how
you're performing it today,

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.080
because I also heard him earlier.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.310
I love it how it's starting,

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.260
I feel like you should release
that version of it as well.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:31.380
It's so great, but what is the reason,

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.292
like why did you need to do this album?

00:10:34.292 --> 00:10:38.580
- Well, I mean, recording
is my favorite thing to do

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.790
other than Broadway, you
know, and doing talk shows.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.090
- Good answer, (all laughing loudly).

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:47.460
- I love making these albums
and you know, the truth is,

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.610
we were almost finished on a
whole other record, you know,

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.560
and then kind of life came

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:57.090
and I went through this
traumatic, you know,

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.280
experience in my life a season.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.660
- Yeah.
- One of those times.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.320
And one, when I got back
to recording, you know,

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.250
I'm sure you've been through this too

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:06.840
you go back to sing those old songs

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:08.490
and you're like, I can't
even sing those anymore.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.323
- [Clarkson] Oh...
- I gotta write.

00:11:09.323 --> 00:11:10.530
- - Yeah.
- All new stuff.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:15.150
So this was just that,
it's really, you know,

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.240
I had the realization
really about journaling

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.970
that whole thing, waking up
an hour and a half earlier,

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.640
all that stuff like, it
was three or four months

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.380
into doing that, that I realized

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:29.730
what I'm actually doing is loving myself.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.980
This is what it looks like, you know.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.120
- Man, (audience clapping
and cheering loudly)

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.530
and if you don't really know that,

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:36.583
like until your eyes are open to that.

00:11:36.583 --> 00:11:37.416
- [Leslie] Yeah.

00:11:37.416 --> 00:11:38.370
- Concept.
- And so this is an album

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.980
sort of about that process,

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:43.530
about that process of firstly learning

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.630
how to love your self you know,

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.232
it's the only way.
- [Clarkson] Yeah.

00:11:47.232 --> 00:11:48.261
- That I have a prayer.

00:11:48.261 --> 00:11:49.261
- 'Cause we're our worst critics, yeah.

00:11:49.261 --> 00:11:50.094
- Oh my God.
- Absolutely.

00:11:50.094 --> 00:11:51.120
- It's the only way that I have a chance

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:56.120
of having grace with my dear
ones, my beloved ones is

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.660
if I have some for myself.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.340
- Absolutely and I don't
know if you can show it

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:01.020
unless you can like, feel it for yourself

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:01.853
as well.
- That's true.

00:12:01.853 --> 00:12:02.686
- Like, you can't project it.

00:12:02.686 --> 00:12:04.020
So your song, that's a good segue

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.040
so it's called "Loved."
- That's right.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.210
- The one you're doing today.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:08.130
Is that kind of the
inspiration behind that?

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:11.430
- Yeah, I, you know,
I was, there's just...

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.980
I'm sure you've had this
too, like, you know,

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:16.770
this realization about
the flexibility of time

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.438
when you have kids.

00:12:18.438 --> 00:12:20.190
You know, there's times
when I'm looking at my son

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.604
and I almost feel like I'm
looking at myself and...

00:12:23.604 --> 00:12:24.437
- Yeah.

00:12:24.437 --> 00:12:26.100
- And I can almost feel, you know,

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.320
it'll be a blink before...
- Oh, I see how...

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.700
- I'm an old man.
- Especially my daughter,

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.080
and I'm like, oh my
God, I can see you at 20

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.170
this is scary.
- Right you know?

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.270
- Yeah.
- And so, anyways,

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.680
it's about that and I was feeling,

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:37.260
you know, kind of connected
to my grandparents,

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:38.640
even though they're no longer here

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.553
and it's about that there's
a refrain in the song.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.900
Show 'em you've been loved,
show 'em how I loved you.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.570
You know, if you've been loved by anybody.

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.440
- Yeah.
- In your life.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:50.340
It's like, you know,

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:52.830
when you're looking for the
courage to take that next step,

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.050
when you're looking at
sometimes the courage to,

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:57.630
you know, go out and face
the world one more time,

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.700
it's like what you, you know,

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.310
if you don't have it within yourself,

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:05.497
I just, I heard my
grandparents saying that,

00:13:05.497 --> 00:13:08.370
"Show the world that we loved you."

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.440
- Yeah and show him what love looks like

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.370
and feels like, yeah,

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.540
(audience clapping and cheering loudly).

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.500
Stay with us everybody,

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.390
because Leslie will be
singing later in the show,

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.950
you do not wanna miss, it's beautiful.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.780
His new album is called
"When a Crooner Dies,"

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:19.653
it's out now.

